kschwethelm/looped-lm-scaling (https://github.com/kschwethelm/looped-lm-scaling)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Kristian Schwethelm. MIT License, see third_party/looped-lm-scaling.LICENSE.
  - src/looptf/optim/muonh.py is adapted from nanochat/optim.py (MuonH with the Polar Express iteration).
  - The transformer block, its initialization, the training recipe and the HyperP learning-rate transfer
    (src/looptf/model/, src/looptf/recipe.py) reimplement nanochat/gpt.py and scripts/base_train.py, and the
    test fixtures in tests/fixtures/ were recorded from that released code.
  That code builds on KellerJordan/modded-nanogpt (MIT) and karpathy/nanochat (MIT).

The Polar Express coefficients are from Amsel et al., "The Polar Express: Optimal Matrix Sign Methods and Their
Application to the Muon Algorithm" (arXiv:2505.16932). The prelude / recurrent block / coda layout follows Geiping
et al., "Scaling up Test-Time Compute with Latent Reasoning: A Recurrent Depth Approach" (arXiv:2502.05171).

Megatron-LM (https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM) is used as a separate checkout under its own license and is
not distributed with this repository.
